e,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1201,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":7608,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-13987](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-13987)\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nYugabyteDB uses the following convention to define the boundary between system attributes and user-defined attributes for a given relation:\r\n - If the relation is backed by YugabyteDB storage, use YBFirstLowInvalidAttributeNumber\r\n - Else use FirstLowInvalidHeapAttributeNumber.\r\n\r\nA helper function YBGetFirstLowInvalidAttributeNumber(relation) is used to make this decision.\r\nThis has the following drawbacks:\r\n - When upstream PG code is merged into Yugabyte, no merge conflict is caused by usages of `FirstLowInvalidHeapAttributeNumber` and so all occurrences of it have to be manually checked and replaced by `YBGetFirstLowInvalidAttributeNumber(rel)`. This causes bugs as in #24641.\r\n - All developers have to be mindful of this distinction and constantly watch out for it.\r\n\r\nThis issue seeks to improve the developer experience by either renaming `FirstLowInvalidHeapAttributeNumber` or replacing it with an ifdef. \r\n\r\n### Issue Type\r\n\r\nkind/enhancement\r\n\r\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\r\n\r\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\r\n\r\n[DB-13987]: https://yugabyte.atla